              Cross-compiling NetHack 5.0 for Atari ST/TT/Falcon
              ===================================================

This document covers the Atari-specific bits of cross-compiling
NetHack 5.0 from a Linux host.  See the top-level Cross-compiling
document for the general theory of NetHack's cross-build (HOST
vs TARGET, the five-step build, etc.).

Cross-compiler used:     Thorsten Otto's m68k-atari-mint-gcc
Cross-compiler url:      https://tho-otto.de/crossmint.php
Author of 5.0 support:   Ingo Paschke


Toolchain
---------

The cross-compiler and its supporting libraries are distributed
as binary tarballs from tho-otto.de.  There are no apt/yum
packages -- you download the .tar.xz / .tar.bz2 archives and
extract them at the host root '/'.  Files land under
/usr/m68k-atari-mint and /usr/lib/gcc/m68k-atari-mint and can
be uninstalled by removing those directories.

Host tools (run on Linux; verified with gcc 15.2.0, builds also
on gcc 14.x).  Download from https://tho-otto.de/crossmint.php:

    gcc-<version>-mint-<date>-bin-linux64.tar.xz
    binutils-<version>-mint-<date>-bin-linux64.tar.xz

Install at /:

    cd /
    sudo tar xJf gcc-<version>-mint-<date>-bin-linux64.tar.xz
    sudo tar xJf binutils-<version>-mint-<date>-bin-linux64.tar.xz


Target libraries
----------------

The Atari build needs three libraries linked into the binary at
build time.  These are TARGET binaries (m68k a.out objects),
distributed as tarballs whose contents go into the cross-mint
sysroot at /usr/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root/.

  C library + headers: mintlib
    https://tho-otto.de/snapshots/mintlib/
    Without this, nothing C-related will link.

  Math: fdlibm
    https://tho-otto.de/snapshots/fdlibm/
    Replaces MiNTLib's libm.a, which has a multiple-definition
    flaw in 'xcpt' that would otherwise require
    -Wl,--allow-multiple-definition at link time.

  GEM AES/VDI bindings: gemlib
    https://tho-otto.de/snapshots/gemlib/
    Provides libgem.a and gem.h.

Install all three INTO the sysroot directory (NOT at /).  The
tarballs include a usr/ prefix that becomes
/usr/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root/usr/...:

    sudo mkdir -p /usr/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root
    cd /usr/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root
    sudo tar xjf <path>/mintlib-<version>-mint.tar.bz2
    sudo tar xjf <path>/fdlibm-<version>-mint.tar.bz2
    sudo tar xjf <path>/gemlib-<version>-mint.tar.bz2

Do NOT extract these tarballs at /: their internal layout uses
usr/include and usr/lib, which would conflict with the host's
Linux libc headers.

  GEM UI toolkit: E_GEM 2.2
    https://github.com/ingpaschke/EGEM_220
    Provides libe_gem.a and e_gem.h -- windows, dialogs,
    popups, sliders, drag-and-drop, XAcc/AV protocols.  The
    makefile has no install target; build and copy by hand:

        git clone https://github.com/ingpaschke/EGEM_220.git
        cd EGEM_220/source
        make -f makefile.gcc
        sudo cp libe_gem.a /usr/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root/usr/lib/
        sudo cp e_gem.h    /usr/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root/usr/include/


Host build prerequisites
------------------------

    sudo apt install make perl zip


Building
--------

On your Linux host, from the top of the NetHack source tree:

    sys/unix/setup.sh sys/unix/hints/linux.500
    make fetch-lua
    make CROSS_TO_ATARI=1 all
    make CROSS_TO_ATARI=1 package

The 'CROSS_TO_ATARI=1' flag activates the Atari hints under
sys/unix/hints/include/cross-*.500, which override TARGET_CC,
TARGET_AR, TARGET_LINK, TARGET_CFLAGS, TARGET_LFLAGS, and the
source/object lists.  The build produces:

    targets/atari/nethack.prg       Atari 68000 m68k-atari-mint
                                    GEM application
    targets/atari/NH500ST.ZIP       Packaged self-contained game
                                    directory (~3 MB) ready to
                                    unzip on the Atari side.

ZIP contents are documented in sys/atari/README.tos.


Notes
-----

  - The cross-build only touches sys/atari/ and win/gem/ plus a
    handful of small #ifdef-guarded additions in the shared core
    (include/extern.h, include/global.h, include/winprocs.h,
    src/{files,mdlib,save,windows}.c, sys/share/pcmain.c).  The
    cross-build hints live in sys/unix/hints/include/cross-pre1.500,
    cross-pre2.500, and cross-post.500.

  - The host-side tools bmp2img_host and img2mono_host are built
    with the host's native compiler and run on the host to convert
    nhtiles.bmp into the three IMG tile sheets (NH16.IMG, NH32.IMG,
    NH2.IMG) that ship in the package.

  - For playing the game and end-user configuration, see
    sys/atari/README.tos.
